    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Camargo area was home to prehistoric mound‑building cultures and later historic tribes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/comargo_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Camargo’s post office opened in 1848 and stayed in service until 1963, operating for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camargo%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Camargo’s climate gives a 201‑day growing season, perfect for corn and tobacco on its surrounding cropland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/comargo_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bowles Branch borders Camargo to the south while Greenbrier Creek runs through its northern part.",
